[node name="HowToText" type="Label" parent="TextData" unique_id=779007317]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 0
text = "GOAL: Survive 5 days, serve at least 15 clients, keep average satisfaction at 75% or higher.

STREET: A/D or arrow keys to walk. E/W/Space in front of a door to enter. Left: Jaya Parts Shop. Right: Workshop. Customers queue on the sidewalk (max 5).

WORKSHOP: Read the client's order and budget. Click a bike part marked * to zoom. Hold-click a part card in the top tray, drag it onto the glowing bike part, then release (or click the card, then click the bike). Install everything ordered, then HAND OVER.

SUDDEN CHANGE: Clients may change their mind once the bike is 100% done. Choose: Accept and lower the tier, Install anyway and take the loss, Refuse outright, or Cut corners (install cheap parts for big profit, but you might get caught!).

SHOP: Click a card to add it to the cart, then BUY. Shop stock changes at 17:00 and every new day, with higher tiers.

TIPS: Matching the ordered tier keeps clients happy. Higher tiers make them very happy but can eat your profit. Used Tier 1 parts on high-tier orders make clients suspicious!
TAB: check stock. ESC or right-click: cancel/exit.

LOSE: average satisfaction 10% or lower, or out of money with no stock."

